<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="lead">
      A great many IT problems don't need anyone in the room. With your
      permission we can connect to your computer over the internet, see what you
      see, and put things right while you watch — often the same day, and
      usually quicker than waiting for a visit.
    </p>

    <h2>What we can sort remotely</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>Slow computers cleaned up and speeded back up</li>
      <li>Windows and software updates, errors and crashes</li>
      <li>Email problems — settings, passwords, mail not sending or arriving</li>
      <li>Viruses, pop-ups and suspicious warnings</li>
      <li>Printers, scanners and devices that have stopped talking to your computer</li>
      <li>Setting up backups, accounts and new software</li>
      <li>One-to-one training and walking you through something step by step</li>
      <li>AI tools set up and explained</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What still needs a visit</h2>
    <p>
      We will always tell you honestly which it is. Anything physical needs us
      there in person: a machine that won't switch on, a broken screen, failing
      hardware, cabling, Wi-Fi that needs moving or testing around the house, or
      a computer that can't get online at all.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-panel">
      <h2>Worried about remote access? Good.</h2>
      <p>
        You should be. Criminals phone people pretending to be from Microsoft,
        BT or a bank and talk them into granting remote access. It is one of the
        most common scams there is, and older people are targeted most.
        <strong>We will never ring you out of the blue asking for access.</strong>
        A genuine session only ever happens when <em>you</em> have contacted
        <em>us</em> and we have agreed it together.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How a remote session works</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li><strong>It starts with you.</strong> Nothing happens until you have contacted us and we have agreed a time together.</li>
      <li><strong>You download a small program from our own website</strong> while we are on the phone or a video call with you. We will tell you the address; it is short enough to say out loud.</li>
      <li><strong>You ask for help, and you give permission.</strong> You click a button to request the session, then a message appears on your screen asking whether to allow it. Nothing happens until you say yes.</li>
      <li><strong>You watch the whole thing.</strong> Your screen stays in front of you and you see every click we make.</li>
      <li><strong>You can stop instantly.</strong> Closing the window ends the connection there and then.</li>
      <li><strong>The connection is encrypted</strong> from your computer to ours.</li>
      <li><strong>Nothing stays behind.</strong> The program does not install itself. Close it when we are finished and it is gone — we cannot reconnect later unless you download it again and approve it again.</li>
      <li><strong>We never need your banking details.</strong> If anyone ever asks you for those during a support session, it is a scam — end it and ring us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Joining a session</h2>
    <p>
      There are two parts, and neither needs an account or a subscription.
      First we talk: sessions you have booked run over Cal Video, which opens in
      your web browser from a link — there is nothing to install for that.
      Then, once we are talking, you download the small helper program from our
      website so we can see your screen.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you would like a record of the work, ask and we will agree how before
      we start. We never record anything without asking you first. See our
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how we handle your information.
    </p>

    <h2>What it costs</h2>
    <p>
      Remote work is charged at the same rates as everything else —
      £{{ site.hourlyRate }} an hour {{ site.vatIncLabel }} for home users and
      £{{ site.businessHourlyRate }} an hour {{ site.vatExLabel }} for business —
      but there is no travel and no waiting for an appointment slot, so smaller
      jobs are often quicker and cheaper. See <a href="/pricing/">full pricing</a>
      or our <a href="/support-plans/">support plans</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Where we can help, and on what</h2>
    <p>
      Our on-site visits cover Penarth, Barry, Cardiff and the surrounding Vale
      of Glamorgan. <strong>Remote support has no such limit</strong> — if you
      have a working internet connection, we can help you anywhere in the UK.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Remote support is for Windows computers.</strong> If you use a Mac
      or Linux we can still help — it is a visit, or something we arrange with
      you directly — so do ask rather than assuming we cannot. We would rather
      say this plainly than have you download something that was never going to
      work.
    </p>

